; Seven `invalid_manifest`s. Three come from `bad-unitless` — one per element
; of `[1 2 3]`, since each is its own bad spelling — then one each for the
; magnitude, the underlying, and the duplicate in each of the two authoring
; shapes.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-unitless members])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-unitless members])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-unitless members])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-magnitude members])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-underlying members])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-duplicate members])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [bad-duplicate-compact members]))
